    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test class \u2014 the only one in the project \u2014 passing).\n\n## Change\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeNewOwner(...)`, a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date now fails validation, which causes `addOwner` to return `400 Bad Request`:\n\n```java\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n    owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());\n} else if (owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\nI placed the check in `normalizeNewOwner` because that is where the controller already funnels its field-level `400` rejections (blank address, invalid telephone, bad postcode) \u2014 `addOwner` maps a `false` return to `HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST`. The check runs only when a date was actually supplied (a missing date still defaults to today) and before `rollToBusinessDay`, so it compares the client-supplied value against the server date as specified. I also updated the method's Javadoc to document the new rejection reason.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` and expecting 400) passes.",
